{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-interaction-discipline", "file": "references/action-only-budget-discipline.md", "content": "# Action-only turns and demo-budget discipline

In constrained Continual-ARC sessions, treat the benchmark's response contract as an execution boundary: each turn must contain exactly one permitted action JSON object and no prose or unrelated tool calls. Keep all puzzle reasoning internal; do not invoke delegation, planning/status utilities, scratch commands, or skill lookups during an active puzzle turn.

After each demo response, compare the complete input and output before deciding the next action. Record object/component coordinates, exact changed cells, unchanged lookalikes, output dimensions, and plausible competing rules. Request another demo only when its possible outcomes discriminate between named hypotheses; repeated demo requests without incorporating the latest pair burn budget without adding evidence. Track demo/submission counts and spend the remaining budget deliberately. Submit once one coherent rule fits every demo and the test; validate dimensions and preserve all unaffected content.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-interaction-discipline/references/action-only-budget-discipline.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/repeated-pattern-output-validation.md", "content": "# Repeated-pattern output validation

When output dimensions are integer multiples of input dimensions, consider tiled-copy as one hypothesis—not a conclusion. Compare every candidate tile cell-by-cell against the original input across all demos. Look for generated motifs, mirrors, rearrangements, and row/column ordering when blocks differ. A simple-repeat guess is falsified by any mismatching tile or incorrect submission; do not retry the same rule with a different output layout. Infer the precise construction from the complete demonstrations, then validate the resulting dimensions and every cell before applying it to the test.
