A 10x10 demonstration has background 4 and a closed rectangular color-6 outline spanning rows 1–7 and columns 0–6. The output leaves the background, outline, and exterior unchanged, and changes only the enclosed interior (rows 2–6, columns 1–5) from 4 to 7. This shows that cavity fill can use a third color distinct from both outline and background. For another instance, identify cavity candidates and infer the exact fill color from current evidence; do not assume every enclosed outline has the same mapping solely from task ID or geometry. The first test answer guessed 7 for several outline colors, but was rejected; the demo only validates fill=7 for the shown color-6-on-4 configuration. The test contains color-5-on-3 and color-6-on-3 enclosures, so this demo alone does not determine their outputs. Analyze subsequent demonstrations before submitting.
