{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-interaction-discipline", "file": "references/outline-color-scope.md", "content": "# Scope validation for outline-filling tasks

A demonstrated fill establishes only that the particular enclosed interior in that pair changes to the observed color. In a fresh grid with multiple closed outlines, especially outlines of different colors or dimensions, do not extrapolate that every cavity is selected. Inventory each cavity and compare boundary color, geometry, and interior against the demonstrated case. Preserve the border and exterior, and change only interiors supported by the rule. If the available demo does not distinguish candidate selectors (for example, one eligible-color outline versus another-color outline), spend a demo request on that ambiguity before submitting.

This lesson arose in a task-67c59573 recurrence: one demo showed a color-6 rectangular outline's background interior becoming 7; the test also included color-5 rectangular outlines. Two submissions filled both types, with differing scope, and were incorrect. The demos did not establish that the color-5 cavities should be filled, so this is a warning about overgeneralization, not a solved selection rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484802/attempts/57865763327545bc884e27f058eb3817/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-interaction-discipline/references/outline-color-scope.md"}
